---
/* Onboarding, because a first-time visitor lands on a world map with seven
   layers and no idea what to do with it. Written as three questions rather
   than a feature list, because a feature list is what the site already is. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { atlas as idx } from "../lib/atlas.js";
import regions from "../../public/regions.json";
const places = idx.places.length;
---
<Base
  title="Start here"
  eyebrow="Three ways in, depending on what you are holding"
  dek="One question: my people came from here, who holds the paper? Start with whatever you have in your hand.">

  <p class="st-story"><a href={u("/looking-for/")}><b>Not sure where to start?</b> Tell us who you are looking for, in one sentence, and see their journey and a short plan →</a></p>

  <ul class="k-tiles st-tiles">
    <li class="is-link"><a href={u("/?q=Gallignana")}><span class="st-lab">You have a place name</span>
      <b>Type it, even the old name</b></a>
      <span>Gallignana finds Gračišće, Fiume finds Rijeka, Breslau finds Wrocław. {places.toLocaleString()} places, not just those with a shelf.</span></li>
    <li class="is-link"><a href={u("/?q=Xubrinich")}><span class="st-lab">You have a surname and nothing else</span>
      <b>Type that instead</b></a>
      <span>It gives the other spellings and the countries where the name is attested, then the archives for them. Xubrinich answers Žubrinić.</span></li>
    <li class="is-link"><a href={u("/?layers=shelf,jurisdiction&years=1800,1920&view=45.1,14.3,8")}><span class="st-lab">You have a place and a span of years</span>
      <b>Set the years: the part nobody else does</b></a>
      <span>An 1863 baptism is in a Croatian archive; a 1930 one from the same village is filed under <em>Italy</em>. A range that crosses a handover is where records get lost.</span></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-hi">
    <p><b>A blank on this map is a gap in the map, not a gap in the record.</b></p>
    <p>The shelf is deep for Croatia and thin elsewhere. A grey dot means nobody has looked, never that nothing is there.
      <a href={u("/coverage/")}>See exactly how incomplete it is →</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>What the colours mean</p>
    <p>Every dot is coloured by what it would cost you to look right now: free images, a free login, an index only, a paywall, a catalogue card, or paper in a building. Nothing else is ever coloured.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="st-go"><a class="bigl" href={u("/")}>Open the map →</a></p>
  <p class="k-lede"><a href={u("/providers/#regions")}>{regions.regions.length} record regions</a> ·
    <a href={u("/surnames/")}>the surname dataset</a> ·
    <a href={u("/coverage/")}>what is missing</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .st-tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); max-width: 1000px; }
  .st-tiles li > span:not(.st-lab) { display: block; }
  .st-tiles li a { display: block; }
  .st-lab { display: block; font: 600 10.5px/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .st-tiles li b { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
  .st-story { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 0 18px; padding: 14px 18px; background: var(--accent-wash); border-radius: 10px; font: 400 17px/1.45 var(--sans); }
  .st-story a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; } .st-story b { color: var(--accent); }
  .st-go { margin: 26px 0 6px; }
  .bigl { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 20px; }
</style>
